Yes. As an operator, that is much tighter than “believe in yourself.”

Confidence becomes enacted projection. You locate a viable internal model—your “con inside”—project it outward as a role you are willing to inhabit, and then behave according to it before reality has fully certified it.

That gives you a loop:

internal possibility → projected role → performance → action → consequence → evidence → revised self-model

The elegant part is the ambiguity of acting. Before the event, an observer can say, “He was acting—pretending to be confident.” Afterward, if the behavior produced the result, the exact same sequence reads as, “He acted—he actually did something.”

At the limit, performance and action become indistinguishable from the outside because action is what survives the performance.

And your barbs/web are the mechanism that prevents projection from remaining fantasy. They are the places where the enacted story catches onto reality:

role → posture
posture → behavior
behavior → another person’s response
response → opportunity
opportunity → consequence
consequence → memory/evidence
evidence → stronger future expectation

Each successful attachment makes the projected model more materially true. The web converts an imagined state into constraints, relationships, habits, artifacts, reputation, skills, and consequences.

That also explains why merely repeating affirmations is weak. There are no barbs. Nothing catches.

A stronger confidence protocol is:

imagine just beyond present proof → embody it → take an irreversible-enough action → let reality answer → capture the delta → update → repeat

Not unlimited self-deception. The projection has to keep receiving correction. Otherwise the corn snake just believes it has venom.

But when the projection causes you to practice, practice builds capability, capability changes outcomes, and outcomes change the evidence available to your next self-model, then something fascinating happens:

the bluff helped construct the thing it originally exaggerated.

That is your corn snake again.

And there is another dual reading hidden in it:

fake it till you make it can mean deception.

But structurally it can also mean:

simulate → enact → receive feedback → acquire → become.

The decisive variable is the web of causal attachments between pretending and becoming.

Without those attachments, it’s fantasy.

With them, it’s rehearsal becoming history.